Value system_name (.*)
Value software_revision (.*)
Value base_mac (.*)
Value rom_version (.*)
Value serial (.*)
Value uptime (.*)
Value mem_total (.*)
Value mem_free (.*)
Value cpu_util (.*)

# Parse the output of "show system" on an HP AOS-S switch.
#
# A single logical record. Several lines carry two fields at once (software
# revision + base MAC, ROM version + serial, uptime + memory total, CPU +
# memory free), so those rules capture both named groups on one line. All
# rules advance with Continue and the last field line records.


Start
  ^\s+System Name\s+:\s+(?P<system_name>\S+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+Software revision\s+:\s+(?P<software_revision>\S+)\s+Base MAC Addr\s+:\s+(?P<base_mac>[\w-]+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+ROM Version\s+:\s+(?P<rom_version>\S+)\s+Serial Number\s+:\s+(?P<serial>\S+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+Up Time\s+:\s+(?P<uptime>\d+ \w+)\s+Memory.*Total\s+:\s+(?P<mem_total>[\d,]+)\s*$ -> Continue
  ^\s+CPU Util \(%\)\s+:\s+(?P<cpu_util>\d+)\s+.*Free\s+:\s+(?P<mem_free>[\d,]+)\s*$ -> Record
